 private val e = listOf(
E("Slow-cooker beef stew","700g braising beef; 2 onions; 3 carrots; 500g potatoes; 500ml beef stock; tomato purée; thyme; flour","Toss beef in flour and brown if desired. Add everything to the cooker, stir and cook until beef and vegetables are tender. Season and serve with bread or mash.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-beef-stew","7–8 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow-cooker sausage casserole","8 pork sausages; 1 onion; 2 carrots; 1 celery stick; 400g chopped tomatoes; 400g cannellini beans; 250ml stock; mixed herbs","Brown sausages if desired. Add all ingredients to the cooker and stir. Cook until sausages are cooked through and vegetables tender. Serve with mash.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-sausage-casserole","6–8 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker chilli con carne","500g beef mince; 1 onion; 1 pepper; 2 garlic cloves; 400g chopped tomatoes; 400g kidney beans; 150ml beef stock; chilli powder; cumin","Brown mince, breaking it up. Add all ingredients to the cooker and stir. Cook until mince is fully cooked and flavours meld. Serve with rice.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-chilli-con-carne","6–8 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow-cooker chicken casserole","8 chicken thighs; 1 onion; 3 carrots; 2 celery sticks; 500ml chicken stock; thyme; bay leaf; 150g peas","Add chicken, chopped vegetables, stock and herbs to the cooker. Cook until chicken is thoroughly cooked and tender. Stir in peas for the final 20 minutes.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-chicken-casserole","6–7 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow-cooker beef stew with dumplings","600g stewing beef; 1 onion; 3 carrots; 2 potatoes; 500ml beef stock; tomato purée; 150g self-raising flour; 75g suet","Cook beef, vegetables, stock and tomato purée until tender. Mix flour and suet with cold water to make a soft dough; form dumplings and cook on top on HIGH for 45–60 minutes until done.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-beef-stew-with-dumplings","7–8 hours on LOW","25 minutes"),
